Responsible-use notice
----------------------
This project is a personal, isolated laboratory for studying how AI agents,
model gateways, and host instrumentation behave during controlled software
installs. It is not a product, not a hosted service, and not permission to
test systems you do not own or operate.

- Run untrusted workloads only inside disposable Lima/QEMU virtual machines.
- Do not place host credentials, cloud keys, or personal files into experiment
  VMs.
- Do not expose model gateways, MCP servers, or observability dashboards to
  the public internet.
- Do not represent a component as exercised unless it actually ran.
- Preserve evidence before deleting a VM. Do not commit secrets.

Third-party software referenced by this repository (Antigravity CLI, Lima,
QEMU, LiteLLM, OmniRoute, Aegis, Numbat, OpenTelemetry, Phoenix, Go, and
security observation tools) remains under its own licenses. This package does
not relicense those projects.

